Date: Tue, 10 Nov 2026 05:19:32 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] firewall4: update to Git HEAD (2026-11-08)

Since the kernel's backport of 871df5007eda ("netfilter: flowtable:
bail out if forward path cannot be discovered"), a flow enters the
flowtable only if the device at the bottom of its forward path is one
of the flowtable's devices. firewall4 of 2026-10-29 lists only the
zone devices for software offloading, so a flow through a bridge finds
its port missing: nft_flow_route() answers -ENOENT for every packet,
and the flow stays on the classic path. firewall4 now lists the devices
below a zone's bridge or VLAN device.

The update also removes the stray template mangle-rule.uc.

3722eadc088c fw4: list the software flowtable devices for hardware offloading too
b25508586879 fw4: list the layer 3 devices of zones in the software flowtable
55e0d749d041 fw4: list the devices a zone names in the software flowtable
a945b12c989f fw4: list lower devices for software flow offloading
d961882bafe8 Revert "fw4: restart in a single nft transaction"
358d42144b72 config: mark unsupported fw3 options correctly
a314df48644e Set has_ports for helper rules and require helper port
4b686774d2a7 templates: remove stray file
7f34d9e0e678 fw4: support multiple ipset references per rule and redirect
daf6cf607cab fw4: reject unknown tokens in ipset references
296ddab860a1 fw4: add WDS ports to the flowtable by prefix
c22c2f241e9e fw4: restart in a single nft transaction
5474da96eb44 ruleset: Add snat_port support for MASQUERADE
613198bebd0b ruleset: avoid no-op port translation in dnat
e497bdcc78f0 config: add dest addr restrictions for DHCPv6 rules
2be5820d470d templates: allow inverted limits
ba2ae80a48c6 firewall4: enable mac ranges for rule
3ab89e865b0d redirect: preserve destination ipsets in NAT reflection
ffa015c64f06 fw4: fix parsing of repeated separators in ipset references
b8a32285c252 fw4: fix misleading family conflict message
466e78ee25a7 fw4: skip protocols a referenced port set does not apply to
40f032c29a0e fw4: skip an include section with invalid options

Signed-off-by: kiritantakechi <kiritantakechi@gmail.com>
